# DL / Vision GPU Performance

When tuning performance:

1. Baseline first: device, precision, batch size, utilization, memory, workers, steps/sec.
2. Classify the bottleneck: compute, memory, input pipeline, or synchronization.
3. Verify device compatibility for model, buffers, generators, indices, and auxiliary tensors.
4. Review throughput knobs: AMP, batch size, accumulation, pinned memory, workers, prefetching, compile mode.
5. Profile before larger refactors.
6. Change one thing at a time and re-measure.

Separate pure throughput changes from training-dynamics changes.
